# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ into dist/, so this ships inside the build
# folder itself — which means it works for a drag-and-drop deploy, where
# netlify.toml (one level up, outside dist) is never read.
#
# Without this, the app loads at "/" but refreshing /about or /pricing returns
# a 404: Netlify looks for a file at that path and there isn't one. React Router
# needs every unknown path handed index.html so it can route on the client.

/*    /index.html   200
